WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.580
Does the peripheral rule hold in the brain and spinal cord?

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.980
Does the axon decide there too?

3
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:15.273
In culture, oligodendrocytes will wrap inert plastic fibers of a suitable diameter.

4
00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:17.693
No axon, and still a wrap.

5
00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:27.367
In mice, Nave's group removed neuregulin-1 and ErbB signaling in the brain and

6
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.027
spinal cord. Myelin still formed.

7
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.190
Yet extra neuregulin from neurons could still thicken central myelin.

8
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.390
The signal can tilt the wrap.

9
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.630
It is not needed to start it.

10
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.070
So in the brain, the glial cell brings much of the program itself.

11
00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.010
Axon cues such as activity, and the caliber of the fiber, bias it.

12
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.780
Zebrafish larvae have transparent spinal cords, so the first sheaths can be filmed

13
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.780
as they form. Most early wraps are withdrawn.

14
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:05.250
Jacob Hines, Bruce Appel and colleagues blocked vesicle release in one axon among

15
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.250
normal neighbours.

16
00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.750
Will oligodendrocytes treat it differently?

17
00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:20.883
Yes. The release-blocked axon was wrapped less often, and its sheaths were shorter.

18
00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:23.803
Release from the axon biases the choice.

19
00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:33.623
In mouse cortex, stimulating neurons with light added new oligodendrocytes and

20
00:01:33.623 --> 00:01:35.083
thickened myelin in that circuit.

21
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.343
These are larval fish and mouse cortex.

22
00:01:39.323 --> 00:01:42.583
Whether such myelin helps adult humans learn is still open.

23
00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:45.203
So the idea has two halves.

24
00:01:46.103 --> 00:01:47.443
In nerve, the axon decides.

25
00:01:48.323 --> 00:01:52.203
In the brain, the glia bring much of the program, and the axon tunes it.
